ing majority voting.' -> self_consistency_selection: majority voting. p.13 exact: 'Here, an external control algorithm is created, that calls the model, each time with a different prompt, so that it follows a tree of reasoning steps. When one reasoning path has been traversed, the search backtracks, and tries an alternative. The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.' -> tot_search: breadth_first, depth_first. Trio: generation prompt + evaluation prompt + external search algorithm; Graph of Thoughts extends; Stream of Search internalizes search by training. p.10-11: interpreter/debugger, PoT, PAL, FunSearch, PDDL planners; long chains risk hallucination, so verification/reflection needed.\",\n  evidence_ids=[\"ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3\",\"ev-4049593a30e2846f8394\"],\n  section=\"reasoning\"\n)", "observations": "Execution logs:\nLast output from code snippet:\n{'note_id': 'reasoning', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'chars': 972}", "observations_images": null, "action_output": {"note_id": "reasoning", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "chars": 972}, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8521, "output_tokens": 392, "total_tokens": 8913}, "is_final_answer": false}}
