use = category 2 acting (pp.20-25): 3.1 World models (model-based RL, vision-language-action models), 3.2 Robots and tools (robot planning, action tools). p.23 exact: 'The Toolformer model is trained to decide which APIs to call, when to call them, what arguments to pass, and how to best incorporate the results into future token prediction. A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar.' -> toolformer_tools: calculator, question_answering, search_engine, translation_system, calendar. Same page exact: 'ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI, a large dataset of publicly available REST APIs.' -> toolbench_api_count: 16464. Related: EasyTool, ToolAlpaca (3938 instances/400 APIs), ToolQA, Gorilla/APIBench. Say Can grounds LLM in robot affordances (101 tasks); Inner Monologue inserts feedback into prompt; planner-caller-summarizer multi-LLM tool pipeline (Shen et al.).\")\n```", "tool_calls": null, "raw": {"_type": "ChatCompletion", "id": "74ff87ca-0915-4af6-825c-e881199e3272", "choices": [{"_type": "Choice", "finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"_type": "ChatCompletionMessage", "content": "Recording the tool_use topic note from page 23 evidence.\n\nThe ToolFormer note: page 23 lists the five tested tools (calculator, question answering, search engine, translation, calendar) and gives ToolBench's 16,464 APIs.\n\n```python\nn = write_note(title=\"tool_use\", section=\"tool_use\", evidence_ids=[\"ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62\"], content=\"Tool use = category 2 acting (pp.20-25): 3.1 World models (model-based RL, vision-language-action models), 3.2 Robots and tools (robot planning, action tools). p.23 exact: 'The Toolformer model is trained to decide which APIs to call, when to call them, what arguments to pass, and how to best incorporate the results into future token prediction. A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering syste