o planning and self-reflection (p.33); LLMs approach or exceed average human social judgment (p.35).\", evidence_ids=[\"ev-e403dfb2811682ecd186\",\"ev-41048209f3096e51f36b\",\"ev-a9b70da77a1c104405a2\",\"ev-345e6706309ac04ee927\"], section=\"multi_agent\")\n```", "code_action": "write_note(title=\"multi_agent\", content=\"Multi-agent interaction = category 3 (pp.33-36). Sect. 4.2 role-based interaction: LLM agents communicate in natural language, enabling game theory, role-play and teamwork research. Strategic behavior in multi-LLM environments: MAgIC uses social deduction games and game-theoretic scenarios, extracting seven features: Rationality, Judgement, Reasoning, Deception, Self-awareness, Cooperation, Coordination (p.35). GPT-o1 and GPT-4 score best; all score lower on Reasoning, most low on Coordination. GAMA-Bench covers Guess 2/3 of the Average, El Farol Bar, Divide the Dollar, Public Goods, Diner's Dilemma, Sealed-bid Auction, Battle Royale and Pirate Game (p.35). AucArena simulates auctions (p.36). Theory of mind supports social interaction and is linked to planning and self-reflection (p.33); LLMs approach or exceed average human social judgment (p.35).\", evidence_ids=[\"ev-e403dfb2811682ecd186\",\"ev-41048209f3096e51f36b\",\"ev-a9b70da77a1c104405a2\",\"ev-345e6706309ac04ee927\"], section=\"multi_agent\")", "observations": "Execution logs:\nLast output from code snippet:\n{'note_id': 'multi_agent', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'chars': 860}", "observations_images": null, "action_output": {"note_id": "multi_agent", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "chars": 860}, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8653, "output_tokens": 1397, "total_tokens": 10050}, "is_final_answer": false}}
