tive Agents (pp.46-47) add memory, planning, reflection modules; quote p.47: 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' -> generative_agents_evaluators: 100. Simulating 1000 People: 1052 interview agents replicate GSS answers 85% as accurately as humans two weeks later; emergent behaviour, plus erratic/hallucinated behaviour observed.\",\n evidence_ids=[\"ev-75546d247dedb90561b5\",\"ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886\"],\n section=\"multi_agent\")\nprint(r)\n```", "tool_calls": null, "raw": {"_type": "ChatCompletion", "id": "07f3b18f-799a-4d66-a016-2291da953fa9", "choices": [{"_type": "Choice", "finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"_type": "ChatCompletionMessage", "content": "Page 47 gives the Generative Agents credibility evaluation: 100 human evaluators, and CAMEL's inception prompt is confirmed on page 46. I'll update the multi_agent note with both answers plus continuous quotes, preserving earlier findings.\n\nNote text: \"Multi-agent interaction = category 3 (Sect. 4, pp.33-47). Role-based interaction: LLM agents exchange natural-language messages (role-play, teamwork, game theory, debate systems such as ChatEval/AutoGen); MAgIC social-deduction games extract Rationality, Judgement, Reasoning, Deception, Self-awareness, Cooperation, Coordination (p.35); Sotopia/GovSim test social goals and cooperation. CAMEL (p.46): user+assistant agents; quote p.46: 'Both agents are given a so-called inception prompt, an initial idea.' -> camel_prompting: inception_prompting. Generative Agents (pp.46-47) add memory, planning, reflection modules; quote p.47: 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' -> generative_agents_evaluators: 100. Simulating 1000 People: 1052 interview agents replicate GSS answers 85% as accurately as humans two weeks later; emergent behaviour, plus erratic/hallucinated behaviour ob