}, "model_output": "Page 47 gives the Generative Agents credibility evaluation: 100 human evaluators, and CAMEL's inception prompt is confirmed on page 46. I'll update the multi_agent note with both answers plus continuous quotes, preserving earlier findings.\n\nNote text: \"Multi-agent interaction = category 3 (Sect. 4, pp.33-47). Role-based interaction: LLM agents exchange natural-language messages (role-play, teamwork, game theory, debate systems such as ChatEval/AutoGen); MAgIC social-deduction games extract Rationality, Judgement, Reasoning, Deception, Self-awareness, Cooperation, Coordination (p.35); Sotopia/GovSim test social goals and cooperation. CAMEL (p.46): user+assistant agents; quote p.46: 'Both agents are given a so-called inception prompt, an initial idea.' -> camel_prompting: inception_prompting. Generative Agents (pp.46-47) add memory, planning, reflection modules; quote p.47: 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' -> generative_agents_evaluators: 100. Simulating 1000 People: 1052 interview agents replicate GSS answers 85% as accurately as humans two weeks later; emergent behaviour, plus erratic/hallucinated behaviour observed.\"\n\n```python\nr = write_note(title=\"multi_agent\",\n content=\"Multi-agent interaction = category 3 (Sect. 4, pp.33-47). Role-based interaction: LLM agents exchange natural-language messages (role-play, teamwork, game theory, debate systems such as ChatEval/AutoGen); MAgIC social-deduction games extract Rationality, Judgement, Reasoning, Deception, Self-awareness, Cooperation, Coordination (p.35); Sotopia/GovSim test social goals and cooperation. CAMEL (p.46): user+assistant agents; quote p.46: 'Both agents are given a so-called inception prompt, an initial idea.' -> camel_prompting: inception_prompting. Generative Agents (pp.46-47) add memory, planning, reflection modules; quote p.47: 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' -> generative_agents_evaluators: 100. Simulating 1000 People: 1052 interview agents replicate GSS answers 85% as accurately as humans two weeks later; emergent behaviour, plus erratic/hallucinated behaviour observed.\",\n evidence_ids=[\"ev-75546d247dedb90561b5\",\"ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886\"],\n section=\"multi_agent\")\nprint(r)\n```", "code_action": "r = write_note(title=\"multi_agent\",\n content=\"Multi-agent interaction = category 3 (Sect. 4, pp.33-47). Role-based interaction: LLM agents exchange natural-language messages (role-play, teamwork, game theory, debate systems such as ChatEval/AutoGen); MAgIC social-deduction games extract Rationality, Judgement, Reasoning, Deception, Self-awareness, Cooperation, Coordination (p.35); Sotopia/GovSim test social goals and cooperation. CAMEL (p.46): user+assistant agents; quote p.46: 'Both agents are given a so-called inception prompt, an initial idea.' -> camel_prompting: inception_prompting. Generative Agents (pp.46-47) add memory, planning, reflection modules; quote p.47: 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' -> generative_agents_evaluators: 100. Simulating 1000 People: 1052 interview agents replicate GSS answers 85% as accurately as humans two weeks later; emergent behaviour, plus erratic/hallucinated behaviour observed.\",\n evidence_ids=[\"ev-75546d247dedb90561b5\",\"ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886\"],\n section=\"multi_agent\")\nprint(r)", "observations": "Execution logs:\n{'note_id': 'multi_agent', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'chars': 969}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone", "observations_images": null, "action_output": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8821, "output_tokens": 1784, "total_tokens": 10605}, "is_final_answer": false}}
