da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:47', 'required': True, 'page': 47, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 5018, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-aa9b9dbdfec8c640b495', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:48', 'required': True, 'page': 48, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4375, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-6e64db9ec6bfa8f9417f', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:49', 'required': True, 'page': 49, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4295, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-42cada09d7411017eb46', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:50', 'required': True, 'page': 50, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4663, 'exposed': False}, {'id': 'ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:51', 'required': True, 'page': 51, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 3844, 'exposed': False}, {'id': 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:52', 'required': True, 'page': 52, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4072, 'exposed': False}], 'notes': {'overview': {'id': 'overview', 'content': \"Agentic LLMs survey (arXiv:2503.23037v3), Plaat et al. Definition p.4: agents that receive natural-language input, reason to make decisions and take autonomous actions. Category framework p.4-5: 'The categories reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other' -> answers categories: reason, act, interact (paper wording reasoning / acting / interacting); category 1 reasoning (reflection, retrieval, decision making), category 2 acting (tools, robots; assistants in medicine/finance), category 3 interacting (multi-agent role-play, open-ended agent societies, emergent behaviour). Literature selection p.5 (Sect. 1.2): 'The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.' -> search_methods: google_scholar_search, snowballing. Only LLM-based work included; non-agentic LLM work used as background; most works 2024, some 2023/2025.\", 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-26c94297c50e4ef408a2', 'ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5'], 'valid': True, 'request': 6}, 'reasoning': {'id': 'reasoning', 'content': \"Reasoning = category 1 (pp.7-8): 2.1 Multi-step, 2.2 Self Reflection, 2.3 Retrieval Augmentation. p.10 exact: 'Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.' -> self_consistency_selection: majority voting. p.13 exact: 'Here, an external control algorithm is created, that calls the model, each time with a different prompt, so that it follows a tree of reasoning steps. When one reasoning path has been traversed, the search backtracks, and tries an alternative. The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.' -> tot_search: breadth_first, depth_first. p.14: 'Self reflection happens when an external algorithm uses the LLM to assess its own predictions, and creates a new prompt for the same LLM to come up with a better answer'; framed as RL where both agent and environment are the LLM with different prompts; needs external memory. p.14-15 PHP, Self Refine (p_gen, p_fb, p_refine), Reflexion (actor/evaluator/reflector), Self Discover, Buffer of Thoughts. p.16 implicit reasoning: Self taught reasoner, DeepSeek-R1/GRPO, RASP program emulation. p.10-11 PoT, PAL, FunSearch, PDDL planners; long chains risk hallucination.\", 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3', 'ev-4049593a30e2846f8394', 'ev-2c5302116a7f6c84effa', 'ev-b8db09947ef7c899cd9d', 'ev-ced75d6936911b2f0248'], 'valid': True, 'request': 10}, 'tool_use': {'id': 'tool_use', 'content': \"Tool use = category 2 acting (pp.20-25). p.23 exact: 'A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar.' -> toolformer_tools: calculator, question_answering, search_engine, translation_system, calendar. p.23 exact: 'ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI, a large dataset of publicly available REST APIs.' -> toolbench_api_count: 16464. p.24: computer/browser tools (OmniParser V2, Computer Use, Operator, Browser Use), interoperability protocols MCP/ACP/ANP/A2A. p.24-25 safety: AgentHarm 110 malicious tasks; Rainbow Teaming quality-diversity adversarial prompts (MAP-Elites). p.25-26 assistants: AssistantGPT (LLM+tools+planner+memory), meeting assistants, MUCA, thinking assistant.\", 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62', 'ev-4e747765f5046c8ad8b1'], 'valid': True, 'request': 14}, 'multi_agent': {'id': 'multi_agent', 'content': \"Multi-agent interaction = category 3 (Sect. 4, pp.33-47). Role-based interaction: LLM agents exchange natural-language messages (role-play, teamwork, game theory, debate systems such as ChatEval/AutoGen); MAgIC social-deduction games extract Rationality, Judgement, Reasoning, Deception, Self-awareness, Cooperation, Coordination (p.35); Sotopia/GovSim test social goals and cooperation. CAMEL (p.46): user+assistant agents; quote p.46: 'Both agents are given a so-called inception prompt, an initial idea.' -> camel_prompting: inception_prompting. Generative Agents (pp.46-47) add memory, planning, reflection modules; quote p.47: 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' -> generative_agents_evaluators: 100. Simulating 1000 People: 1052 interview agents replicate GSS answers 85% as accurately as humans two weeks later; emergent behaviour, plus erratic/hallucinated behaviour observed.\", 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-75546d247dedb90561b5', 'ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886'], 'valid': True, 'request': 23}}}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone", "observations_images": null, "action_output": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8579, "output_tokens": 164, "total_tokens": 8743}, "is_final_answer": false}}
